From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:44:21 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 67/79] flashnext_mia: lane costs kept between loads
 (lanes.cost_cache), timed only when a rank has none

A start timed the lane costs every load (2 passes of 4 warm + 9 timed rounds per width, ~39 s). The table now
goes to lanes.cost_cache under a key of the build, the GPU (name, compute capability, SMs, driver), the rank, the
settings both ranks agreed on and the environment's speed entries (TF_FLASHNEXT_, TF_TP_, TF_CUDA_, TF_ROCE_,
NCCL_, CUDA_). Both ranks take the kept table only when both hold one that fits the lane set (link.both); else
both time it as before and keep it. The costs line says kept or measured.
